<title>FRANCE: U.S tops Paris airports export destination in June.</title>
<headline>U.S tops Paris airports export destination in June.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. was the main destination for export traffic from the Paris airports in June 1997, the Paris airport authority (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>June 1997 export traffic via Charles de Gaulle and Orly totalled 52,494 tonnes, an increase of 1.3 percent on the same period last year it added.</p>
<p>The 20 top destinations with percentage change on June 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>    Origin		tonnes     Percent</p>
<p>					   Change 1996</p>
<p>    1. United States  12,177  down  4.0</p>
<p>    2. Japan	     2,670    up  0.4</p>
<p>    3. Hong Kong	 2,636    up 17.1</p>
<p>    4. Canada	    2,036    up 15.5</p>
<p>    5. Germany	   1,893    up 17.4</p>
<p>    6. UK		  1,556    up 18.1</p>
<p>    7. Brazil	    1,547    up 34.1</p>
<p>    8. India	     1,451    up  2.4</p>
<p>    9. U.A.E.	    1,302  down 16.5</p>
<p>   10. Mexico	    1,064    up  4.2</p>
<p>   11. Fr.W.Indies     1,050    up  4.3</p>
<p>   12. Singapore	 1,044    up 28.5</p>
<p>   13. Reunion	     891    up  5.2</p>
<p>   14. China		 847    up 29.2</p>
<p>   15. Egypt		 830    up 12.8</p>
<p>   16. Saudi Arabia	739    up  8.5</p>
<p>   17. Italy		 625  down 26.6</p>
<p>   18. Thailand	    603  down 11.8</p>
<p>   19. Korea		 598  down 15.4</p>
<p>   20. Lebanon	     574  down 10.1</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
